{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571647089,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MjcyODc4NjQ1MA=="},"title":"`git status` broken in submodule with adjusted branch","was":"`git status` broken in submodule with adjusted branch (on crippled FS)"},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571647101,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MjcyODc4NzA0NQ=="},"title":"`git status` broken in submodule with adjusted branch (on crippled FS)","was":"`git status` broken in submodule with adjusted branch"},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571647107,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDI3Mjg3ODczNDk="},"added":["severity-normal"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1571673001,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NDU3ODQwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3820#issuecomment-544578408"},"message":"I have not been able to reproduce this using git-annex on FAT w/o\ndatalad. I guess it has something to do with the .git file/symlink in\nthe submodule confusing git so it does not always treat it as a git\nrepository, or something like that.\n\nI did find a bug in git-annex init in this situation, that prevented it\nfrom entering an adjusted branch in the submodule if the submodule\nwas cloned from a repo with the same adjusted branch checked out.\nFixed in commit fc7c6a5a33df7c33274c79bbe635b8ad082d5436.\nI don't think you encountered this bug though.\n\nIt seems that git status will always report a submodule to be modified\nwith \"(new commits)\" when a different commit is checked out; it does not\ncare that the submodule's master branch is unchanged. I don't see a way\naround that, unfortunately.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571744168,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NDkyMDI5Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3820#issuecomment-544920292"},"message":"Thanks @joeyh \n\n\u003e I have not been able to reproduce this using git-annex on FAT w/o datalad. I guess it has something to do with the .git file/symlink in the submodule confusing git so it does not always treat it as a git repository, or something like that.\n\nGood point, it made me realize that this wasn't vfat, but exfat. Here are the respective excerpts for this device and a fat usb drive in comparison on the system in question:\n\n```\n% mount\n...\n/dev/sdb2 on /media/mih/playwithme type fuseblk (rw,nosuid,nodev,relatime,user_id=0,group_id=0,default_permissions,allow_other,blksize=4096,uhelper=udisks2)\n/dev/sdc1 on /media/mih/7CE3-AFF6 type vfat (rw,nosuid,nodev,relatime,uid=1000,gid=1000,fmask=0022,dmask=0022,codepage=437,iocharset=ascii,shortname=mixed,showexec,utf8,flush,errors=remount-ro,uhelper=udisks2)\n\n% sudo blkid -o list\ndevice                       fs_type     label        mount point                      UUID\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n/dev/sdb2                    exfat                   /media/mih/playwithme              545F-616E\n/dev/sdc1                    vfat                     /media/mih/7CE3-AFF6             7CE3-AFF6\n```\n\n\u003e I did find a bug in git-annex init in this situation, that prevented it from entering an adjusted branch in the submodule if the submodule was cloned from a repo with the same adjusted branch checked out. Fixed in commit fc7c6a5a33df7c33274c79bbe635b8ad082d5436. I don't think you encountered this bug though.\n\nI agree, this sounds different. but thanks for fixing it before it hit me! ;-)\n\n\u003e It seems that git status will always report a submodule to be modified with \"(new commits)\" when a different commit is checked out; it does not care that the submodule's master branch is unchanged. I don't see a way around that, unfortunately.\n\nI was expecting that. I think we can ultimately work around it in `datalad status`, but I don't see a way to make it compatible with `git status`.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1571783420,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTE4MzcwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3820#issuecomment-545183700"},"message":"Michael Hanke wrote:\n\u003e Good point, it made me realize that this wasn't vfat, but exfat.\n\nI'm seeing the same behavior with exfat as vfat.\n\ngit version 2.23.0\ngit-annex version: 7.20191018-gb94f2c18e\n\nMust be something else I'm missing to replicate the problem.\nAnyway, looking at the submodule's .git is the obvious thing to do to\nget at why git status is not treating it as a git repo.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571812960,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU0NTI5MzcxNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3820#issuecomment-545293715"},"message":"Erm, grrr... `git submodule init` obviously must be followed by `git submodule update`, otherwise there will be not submodule cloned. No submodule makes `git status` not see a submodule, because there is none.\n\n:man_facepalming: \n\nSorry for the noise.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1571812960,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjczNTgwNjExMQ=="},"status":2}]}